fact WorkItem(id: "WI-372", description: some(value: "Eliminate the term-body rule-DeBruijn-assertion path: route all rule construction through the occurrence-native path (assert_rule_debruijn_with_nodes / finalize_rule_debruijn_nodes), so rule BODIES are materialized + DeBruijn-closed in exactly ONE place. Delete assert_rule_debruijn (4 prod callers: synthesize_conjunction_rule execute.rs, induction-emit load.rs:6676, eq+external-row-bridge load.rs:7363/1505; +7 test callers), assert_rule_debruijn_in_frame (1 prod: cli prove.rs:697 — needs a node-path seed_globals/shared-frame variant), finalize_rule_debruijn (term-side body DeBruijn closure), and assert_rule_with_nodes (its Option<body_nodes> branch). Add a single term->occurrence converter term_body_to_nodes(&[TermId])->Vec<NodeOccurrence> (= the former None-branch materialize-map) used by assert_rule (keeps its term signature; callers untouched) + the migrated synthesis sites. NOTE payoff is CONSOLIDATION, not deletion of the materializer: materialize_from_handle STAYS (typer typing.rs:1417, eval mod.rs:711, smt-gen x4, loader fallback load.rs:5607, assert_rule). KEY RISK: DeBruijn-index equivalence — the term path runs term_to_debruijn on the body then materializes; the node path materializes Global-var occurrences then node_to_debruijn-closes. collect_occurrence_global_vars_ordered is DESIGNED to mirror collect_vars_rec's first-occurrence order (node_occurrence.rs:1581), and the loader already relies on this, so indices match by design — but SMT-gen var_<i> naming + resolve tests must stay green to confirm. User-requested 2026-06-03 (single rule-construction path) after WI-348; assert_fact/assert_rule keep term signatures (route via assert_rule, not the debruijn path). Context: RuleEntry.body:Vec<TermId> already dropped (body_nodes only, WI-246); main source loader already native (load.rs:7053 build_body_atom_occurrence)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-03T20:08:54Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-372", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-06-03 (committed 745051b). Single rule-construction path: term-body rule DeBruijn asserters retired. DELETED assert_rule_debruijn / assert_rule_debruijn_in_frame / finalize_rule_debruijn / assert_rule_with_nodes(Option branch) + the already-orphaned terms_to_debruijn / collect_rule_vars / collect_head_body_vars. ADDED term_body_to_nodes (single materialize_from_handle converter = former None-branch) + assert_rule_debruijn_with_nodes_in_frame (shared-frame prop-031 variant). assert_rule keeps its term signature (callers untouched), internally -> assert_rule_nodes(term_body_to_nodes(body)). Migrated: synthesize_conjunction_rule, induction emitter, eq+external-row-bridge rules, cli structured-proof step synth (prove.rs), 7 test helpers. materialize_from_handle STAYS (typer/eval/smt-gen/assert_rule). Payoff = consolidation (-89 lines, ONE rule-DeBruijn-closure), NOT materializer deletion (as scoped — user accepted the cosmetic-vs-structural tradeoff). DeBruijn-equivalence verified by construction (collect_occurrence_global_vars_ordered mirrors collect_vars_rec over materialized occs; materialize/node_to_debruijn commute) AND empirically (SMT-gen var_<i> naming, induction, structured-proof suites). 1434 green; /code-review clean (0 correctness/2 finders; 3 doc/dead-code findings applied incl. deleting the orphaned terms_to_debruijn pair).", at: "2026-06-03T20:08:54Z")
